The equation is \(\sqrt[20]{x^{\log_{2026}x}} = 26x\). Rewriting gives \(x^{(\log_{2026}x)/20} = 26x\). Let \(t = \log_{2026}x\), so \(x = 2026^t\). Substituting yields \(2026^{t^2/20} = 26 \cdot 2026^t\), or \(2026^{t^2/20 - t} = 26\). Taking \(\log_{2026}\) of both sides gives \(\frac{t^2}{20} - t = \log_{2026}26\). Multiplying by 20: \(t^2 - 20t - 20\log_{2026}26 = 0\). This quadratic has two real roots \(t_1, t_2\) with sum \(t_1 + t_2 = 20\). The corresponding \(x\)-values are \(x_i = 2026^{t_i}\), so their product is \(P = 2026^{t_1 + t_2} = 2026^{20}\).

Factor \(2026 = 2 \times 1013\) (both primes). Thus \(P = 2^{20} \cdot 1013^{20}\). The number of positive integer divisors of \(P\) is \((20+1)(20+1) = 21 \times 21 = 441\).

\boxed{441}
